# Weekly reflections: Samuel Furneaux

Last updated: 13/11/2026.

## Introduction
This file contains the weekly reflections for my contributions to the group project, a self evaluation of my performance and my thoughts on the presentations from other teams for this project.

## Weekly Logs

### Week 1 (w/c 5th October)
**Context:** Group project week one. During this week we received the first group task (creation of a dashboard using Fitbit data) and met as a group for the first time.
**Overview of team meeting:** During the meeting we reviewed the task, identified our deliverables, initiated the GitHub repository for the team and started to discuss roles. We agreed that at the next meeting we should provide an overview of our EDA and undertake a Crazy 8s session for dashboard ideation.
**Next steps:** During the meeting we agreed that our next step would be to undertake the exploratory data analysis (EDA) of the 18 files provided to us. To ensure efficiency and develop a familiarity with the data we agreed to divide up the files between us.
**My contribution during the week:** Before the meeting I proposed that we have a rotating chair and note taker. Firstly, a chair is important for the smooth running of a team meeting and a rotating chair gives each member the opportunity to have that experience. The team agreed to the proposition of a rotating chair and we produced a rota, however the note taker was replaced with each meeting being transcribed and summarised by AI.

### Week 2 (w/c 12th October)
**Context:** Group project week two. Our main focus for this week was to undertake our EDAs of the data allocated to us and prepare for a short presentation of our findings. During this week we also had a lecture on how to articulate good software requirements.
**Overview of team meeting:** The first half of the meeting was dedicated to each member providing a short presentation of their EDA. The second half was dedicated to a Crazy 8s ideation session, producing ideas for features of our dashboard. After which each member discussed an idea or two which they wished to share with the group. We ultimately agreed upon six ideas worth exploring further.
**Next steps:** Each colleague was required to draft a minimum of five requirements against the six features identified.
**My contribution during the week:** My main contribution during this week was to undertake the EDA of my allocated data. 

### Week 3 (w/c 19th October)
**Context:** Group project week 3. This week I was chair for the team meeting. We were also suddenly informed that the deadline for our work would be the next week, as a result before the meeting I created a communal document for each member to identify our deliverables, agree upon the minimum viable product and assign tasks. At short notice I also offered to write up a summary of our EDA as a submission.
**Overview of team meeting:** We started the meeting by reviewing the communal document - this served as a really useful tool to understand the outstanding work and assign tasks to members with deadlines. I also briefly presented my EDA to the team so that they can familiarise themselves with the document and review it for any errors introduced by my summarisation of their work.
**Next steps:** During the meeting we assigned sub-tasks of our features to produce for the Streamlit app and to contribute to the communal script for the group video. My feature was a wellness tracker, providing the user with a simple visual to track their progress against three goals: steps, calories burned and hours slept.
**My contribution during the week:** As chair I also provided an agenda the day before the team meeting to let my colleagues prepare for the meeting.

### Week 4 (w/c 26th October)
**Context:** This week the main objective for the team was to develop a prototype of our dashboard for our presentation. Each member was tasked with producing their own visualisation and then integrating it into the Streamlit app. 
