## Self evaluation
### Overview
As a team we were able to deliver the minimum viable product (a working dashboard, with an EDA summary and a presentation) within the timeframe. I believe we worked well as a team making good use of our meetings and group chat on Teams to keep others updated on our progress and agree on next steps - an example of this is when we were suddenly informed of the delivery date - we were able to meet the next day to agree on the minimum requirements and the steps needed to get us there. As an individual I believe I played a key role in supporting the team with this work.

### My contributions
At the start of the project we didn't set specific roles (e.g., data engineer, project manager or data analyst), this was to allow each member to get experience in each field. As a result I was able to contribute to various aspects of the project:
* EDA - I was responsible for merging everyone's EDA into a single coherent document.
* Meeting chair - I chaired a meeting - setting the agenda, managing times and providing a summary of tasks at the end. 
* Subset of software requirements - I wrote several requirements for the product that it had to meet.
* Wellness tracker app - I wrote the code and developed the visuals for the wellness tracker app as part of the dashboard.
* Presentation - I provided the introduction to the project, the team and a summary of the EDA undertaken. 
* General support - I ensured I was always available to support other colleagues with their work if something popped up and meant they were too busy to contribute that week. I also helped my colleagues debug their errors.

### Strengths
* **Collaboration** I think the team excelled at collaboration (including myself). Our frequent meetings, use of Microsoft Teams and GitHub as well as our setting of clear objectives for each team member meant we were able to collaborate effectively. 
* **Adaptability** I think I was able to demonstrate my adaptability when I offered to undertake the summary of the EDA at short notice, balancing that priority against my other tasks and work.

### Improvements
* **Use of GitHub** I think this project highlighted a gap in my skillset when it comes to the use of GitHub, having to rely upon others to demonstrate how to use several features such as merge requests. This is an area I need to work on before the main project next year. 
* **Team roles** As previously mentioned, in this project we didn't assign specific roles to each member. I think given the nature of this work (i.e., it was a demo) that choice was fine. However, for the main group project I believe setting roles will be key towards ensuring an efficient team.

